also all electrical power.

11:26.960 --> 11:29.160
And I've heard conflicting
reports

11:29.160 --> 11:33.640
anywhere between 1,400 feet on
final approach.

11:33.640 --> 11:35.840
Now, this is something we
actually trained for.

11:37.040 --> 11:40.160
You know, well, not necessarily
for a full electrical failure,

11:40.160 --> 11:42.480
but we certainly trained for
coming up short

11:42.480 --> 11:43.880
because of an engine failure.

11:43.880 --> 11:47.800
And that was pretty consistent I
thought with what I saw.

11:47.800 --> 11:50.720
But, you know, what we're
getting news wise,

11:50.720 --> 11:54.840
just really bugs the crap out of
me because, well, you know,

11:54.840 --> 11:56.120
